# 1640s pike (2026-10-18): a hedge of points. Stands against horse; goes in at push of pike when
# the enemy foot are close, wavering or busy with our shot.
drill "Pike Block"
era 1640s
about "A hedge of points: stands fast against horse, keeps by the shot, and goes in at push of pike when enemy foot come close or waver."
type Pikeman
dials aggression 0.55 discipline 0.85 cohesion 0.95 cover 0.00 patience 0.50 nerve 0.80

sergeant:
  when horse charging                                       -> hold; form tight; stand fast
  when enemy mounted and enemy within 30                    -> hold; form tight; stand fast
  when enemy breaking or enemy broken                       -> charge
  when enemy on foot and enemy within 25                    -> charge; form tight
  when neighbour engaged and enemy on foot and enemy within 50 -> advance; form tight
  otherwise                                                 -> advance slow; form tight

man:
  when enemy horse and enemy within 8                       -> hold
  otherwise                                                 -> follow sergeant
